1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,800
Every Saturday, before the sun was up, my grandmother walked to the market.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:14,800
She was twenty years old. The basket on her head held everything we had to sell.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,510
Eggs from our hens. Coffee from the tree behind the house.

4
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:22,800
Not much, but it was ours.

5
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:30,800
Three hours there. Three hours back. She never once let the basket fall.

6
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:37,800
At the market she bargained like a merchant twice her age.

7
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:45,800
She always said: a soft word sells more coffee than a loud voice.

8
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:53,800
Every coin went into a cloth pouch. That pouch paid for my father's school books.

9
00:00:54,400 --> 00:01:00,800
She came home in the dark, tired, and proud.

10
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:09,800
I have never walked that road. But every step I take today, I take on hers.
